      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2.1 Location and Extent"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The physical geography of Arunachal Pradesh is categorized into three main Himalayan zones: Outer, Middle, and Trans-Himalayan.",
        "The Outer Himalayan Zone comprises the Foothills and the Siwalik Range.",
        "The Trans-Himalayan Zone represents the Greater Himalayas within the state's geography.",
        "Key geographic study components include location, extent, major rivers, climate, districts, mountain peaks, and mountain passes (La)."
      ],
      "id": "owf261c"
    },
